hypotheses.statement:
The strongly convergent descent spectral sequence $$\label{wimg:morava-page}
 E_2^{s,q}=H^s_{\mathop{\mathrm{cts}}}(\mathbb G_a;(E_a)_q)
 \Longrightarrow\pi_{q-s}B_a$$ has the separated homotopy filtration $$\label{wimg:actual-filtration}
 F^s\pi_*B_a
 =\mathop{\mathrm{im}}\bigl(\pi_*I_a^{\otimes_a s}
       \xrightarrow{(\epsilon_a^{\otimes_a s})_*}\pi_*B_a\bigr),
 \qquad I_a^{\otimes_a0}=B_a.$$ Its successive quotients are $E_\infty^{s,*}$ with the usual total degree, and $F^rF^s\subseteq F^{r+s}$.

For $r\geq0$, let $$Z_r=L_{K(a)}(E^{\wedge(r+1)}).$$ For every finite ordinary $p$-local spectrum $W$, there are natural graded isomorphisms $$\label{wup:tested-functions}
 \pi_*(Z_r\wedge W)
 \cong C_{\mathop{\mathrm{cts}}}(\mathbb G_a^r,\pi_*(E\wedge W)).$$ The first $E$-factor acts by constant coefficients.

outputs.exact_statement:
The strongly convergent descent spectral sequence $$\label{wimg:morava-page}
 E_2^{s,q}=H^s_{\mathop{\mathrm{cts}}}(\mathbb G_a;(E_a)_q)
 \Longrightarrow\pi_{q-s}B_a$$ has the separated homotopy filtration $$\label{wimg:actual-filtration}
 F^s\pi_*B_a
 =\mathop{\mathrm{im}}\bigl(\pi_*I_a^{\otimes_a s}
       \xrightarrow{(\epsilon_a^{\otimes_a s})_*}\pi_*B_a\bigr),
 \qquad I_a^{\otimes_a0}=B_a.$$ Its successive quotients are $E_\infty^{s,*}$ with the usual total degree, and $F^rF^s\subseteq F^{r+s}$.

For $r\geq0$, let $$Z_r=L_{K(a)}(E^{\wedge(r+1)}).$$ For every finite ordinary $p$-local spectrum $W$, there are natural graded isomorphisms $$\label{wup:tested-functions}
 \pi_*(Z_r\wedge W)
 \cong C_{\mathop{\mathrm{cts}}}(\mathbb G_a^r,\pi_*(E\wedge W)).$$ The first $E$-factor acts by constant coefficients. The two-factor evaluation is multiplication after $1\wedge g$. In the cumulative coordinates $1,g_1,g_1g_2,\ldots,g_1\cdots g_r$ on the factors, these isomorphisms identify every coface and codegeneracy of the unit Amitsur object with the continuous inhomogeneous group-cochain operator.*


*Consequently, apply the exact ordinary functor $F(V_0,-)$, for a finite ordinary $p$-local spectrum $V_0$, to the full unit Amitsur tower for $E_a$ in $\mathcal C_a$. In the page convention of Proposition <a href="#prop:pages" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:pages">20</a>, its second page is $$\label{wup:cochain-page}
 E_2^{s,q}
 =H^s_{\mathop{\mathrm{cts}}}\bigl(\mathbb G_a,\pi_q(E_a\wedge D V_0)\bigr),
 \qquad D V_0=F(V_0,S).$$ Here $H^s_{\mathop{\mathrm{cts}}}$ means the cohomology of continuous cochains with the adic topology on the indicated coefficient module.

Let $D_0$ be an ordinary right $E$-module for which $\pi_*D_0\otimes_{O_*}(-)$ is exact on finitely generated graded $O_*$-modules. The natural comparison $$\label{wup:relative-base-change}
 \pi_*D_0\otimes_{O_*}\pi_*(E\wedge W)
 \longrightarrow \pi_*(D_0\wedge W)$$ is an isomorphism for every ordinary $p$-local spectrum $W$.*


*For every profinite set $T$, the functor $C_{\mathop{\mathrm{cts}}}(T,-)$ is exact on finitely generated $O$-modules with their $\mathfrak m$-adic topologies. For every finitely generated graded $O_*$-module $M_*$, the natural map is an isomorphism $$\label{wup:function-tensor}
 C_{\mathop{\mathrm{cts}}}(T,O_*)\otimes_{O_*}M_*
 \xrightarrow{\ \cong\ } C_{\mathop{\mathrm{cts}}}(T,M_*).$$ The functions and the displayed graded isomorphism are understood degreewise.
